Fixed. Bug was in `src/import_merge.ts:7` — the duplicate check used `b.url === inc.url`, which is case-sensitive, so `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` weren't recognized as the same URL.

The fix compares only the hostnames case-insensitively via a `sameUrl` helper (using the `URL` API), while leaving the path/query/fragment casing intact. If either URL fails to parse, it falls back to an exact string comparison.

Verified:
- Existing test suite passes (3 passed).
- Direct check: existing `https://example.com/a` + incoming `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` now collapses to 1 entry with unioned tags `["x","y"]`.


